===== PUBLIC_HELDOUT_PREPARATION_ONLY_NO_PRIVATE_PAYLOAD RAW_SHA256=dd011546b97707fe35aa376a30fb4eddeb3ab04354bb2c969ecbaf98081b0bbc RAW_BYTES=3929 [VERBATIM] =====
# Fresh reserved corpus — invocation and comparison contract

This independently prepared protocol covers Semctx #365 T00/R0. The new public receipt commits a fresh private schema-1 manifest. No candidate or observer has been invoked on this corpus. Historical receipts and freezes are not reused.

The oracle is official TypeScript Compiler API 5.9.3, independently acquired with npm SHA512 integrity verified. The product reference is baseline 3e94997fcbefa72ad4d49b2cad180ee79b7c0a9b. Every expected entry has a private CompilerAPI calculation and public baseline rule/interface justification. No Semctx output supplies an expected value.

The receipt fixes 23 cases, 26 variants and eight additive primary families. Each private unit has one or two raw/primitive requests, nonempty exact checks and gaps=[]. Private ids, compositions, source projections and expected values remain local. No input, expectation, count or comparison adaptation is permitted after opening.

Raw requests explicitly supply cwd, case_sensitive, options, retained and qualified. The frozen materializer validates relative files, writes a fresh workspace, makes file/root paths absolute and supplies cwd/case_sensitive. sdk_directory is literally /sdk/lib on both lanes. The identical SDK descriptor must have SHA256 d1e98c4875cc3d1fe302edea4964aa12a58b391a25e6368c800413d45386b654. Its100 library texts were verified against the official5.9.3 archive. Physical descriptor paths may differ; virtual mappings may not.

The public parseNativeHoldout function must accept the exact manifest bytes committed by the receipt. This corpus uses only mode=eq and actual_transform=none. Targets use object keys, array indices or a unique path selector. Missing/ambiguous targets fail. Selected values and arrays are compared exactly, including ordering, field presence and multiplicity. Filters and post-opening translations are forbidden.

Each reason projection binds its target to a named baseline operation and public source authority. Every semantic/module-configuration component also requires executed=true and unsupported=[] for the same observation. Unit PASS additionally requires request/input binding, applicable capability checks and consumed-read provenance. Primitive responses remain bound to the exact operation, descriptor and artifact. No property PASS grants overall admission.

The frozen public holdout runner and its holdout-contract.md retain their strict process, report, confidentiality and joint-intersection guards. Their source hashes, together with comparator/schema source hashes, are recorded in the new receipt.

Before opening, the coordinator must create a new final freeze binding this contract, the new receipt and private manifest commitment, runner, Bun1.4.3 runtime identities, candidate source/artifact, observer, helper, transport fixture and identical SDK descriptor bytes for each platform. No rebuild or comparator adaptation is permitted after this freeze.

The invocation interface is:

`bun <frozen-runner> <private-committed-manifest> <fresh-private-output-directory> <new-public-receipt> <new-final-freeze> <macos|linux>`

The runner invokes the frozen observer once with `suite_replay::suite_phase_a_replay_requires_frozen_manifest --exact --nocapture`, the frozen helper, GOPORT_LIB_PARSE_SNAPSHOT=0, GOPORT_LIB_SNAPSHOT=0 and RUST_TEST_THREADS=1. Detailed outputs remain private. An exposed set is never retried as reserved evidence. Integrity refusal, format failure, execution unavailability and semantic mismatch remain distinct.

Mac/Linux results stay separate. Joint results require the same ordered private ids, manifest and frozen identities, and use the intersection of PASS results. Native Windows and all240 R0 obligations remain separate, unwaived requirements. This projection does not establish whole-project closure, Git/diff/index freshness, test execution or global qualified admission.


===== TRUSTED_FRESH_AUDIT_EVENT_PARSER RAW_SHA256=31c8a31c2682799a9cef0bc0b6fcfccca1b75dd4462669620f4a0c024509e87c RAW_BYTES=14437 [VERBATIM] =====
"""Replay the existing admission and prepare a clean-room Codex review."""

import argparse
import copy
import hashlib
import json
from pathlib import Path
import subprocess
import tempfile


HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
CODEX = Path.home() / ".local/bin/codex"
GATE = Path.home() / ".local/bin/semctx-proof-admission"
GATE_SHA256 = "18b9aada76e3122d4b361fd7d6e2244cdadac4de46601ad029eedfa5b825f512"
DEFAULT_CASE_SHA256 = "993b2957aa5768403c11b6f25b1054c962644ac33857a2f0c99fb7457cf125f0"
CODEX_VERSION = "codex-cli 0.171.0"
MODEL = "gpt-6.2-sol"
PLAN_TOOL = ("functions.request_user_input",)
DISABLED_FEATURES = (
    "memories", "shell_tool", "unified_exec", "multi_agent", "multi_agent_v2",
    "apps", "plugins", "code_mode_host", "computer_use", "browser_use",
    "browser_use_external", "in_app_browser", "image_generation", "tool_suggest",
    "skill_search", "sleep_tool", "view_image", "goals",
)


def digest(data):
    return hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()


def read_pin(root, pin):
    path = (root / pin["path"]).resolve(strict=True)
    if not path.is_relative_to(root.resolve()) or not path.is_file():
        raise ValueError(f"input outside evidence directory: {path.name}")
    data = path.read_bytes()
    if digest(data) != pin["sha256"]:
        raise ValueError(f"SHA-256 differs: {path.name}")
    return data


def verify_tool_inventory(items):
    if not isinstance(items, list) or any(not isinstance(item, dict) for item in items):
        raise ValueError("review inventory is not a prompt item list")
    names = []
    for item in items:
        if item.get("type") == "additional_tools":
            for namespace in item["tools"]:
                if namespace.get("type") != "namespace":
                    raise ValueError("unexpected review tools outside a namespace")
                for tool in namespace["tools"]:
                    if tool.get("type") != "function":
                        raise ValueError("unexpected review tools with a non-function type")
                    names.append(f'{namespace["name"]}.{tool["name"]}')
    if tuple(names) != PLAN_TOOL:
        raise ValueError(f"unexpected review tools: {names}")
    return tuple(names)


def capture(argv, *, cwd, data=None, timeout=35):
    return subprocess.run(argv, cwd=cwd, input=data, capture_output=True, timeout=timeout)


def checked(result, label):
    if result.returncode:
        diagnostic = result.stderr.decode("utf-8", "replace").strip().splitlines()
        detail = diagnostic[-1] if diagnostic else "no diagnostic"
        raise ValueError(f"{label} failed ({result.returncode}): {detail}")
    return result.stdout


def load_case(path, expected_sha256):
    data = path.read_bytes()
    if digest(data) != expected_sha256:
        raise ValueError("case manifest SHA-256 differs")
    config = json.loads(data)
    if type(config.get("schema")) is not int or config["schema"] != 1:
        raise ValueError("unsupported proof case schema")
    inputs = {key: read_pin(path.parent, pin) for key, pin in config["inputs"].items()}
    return json.loads(inputs["epoch"]), inputs


def capture_gate(argv, cwd):
    if digest(GATE.read_bytes()) != GATE_SHA256:
        raise ValueError("installed admission launcher SHA-256 differs")
    result = capture(argv, cwd=cwd)
    if digest(GATE.read_bytes()) != GATE_SHA256:
        raise ValueError("installed admission launcher changed during the check")
    return result


def freeze(epoch):
    subject = epoch["subject"]
    repository = Path(epoch["repository"]).resolve(strict=True)
    argv = [
        str(GATE), "epoch", "--repository", str(repository),
        "--base", subject["base_sha"], "--head", "HEAD",
    ]
    if subject["include_worktree"] is not True:
        raise ValueError("expected an epoch for the complete worktree")
    argv.append("--include-worktree")
    current = checked(capture_gate(argv, repository), "freeze")
    if json.loads(current) != epoch:
        raise ValueError("current candidate or policy differs from the frozen epoch")
    return argv


def gate_check(root, epoch, label, receipt_bytes, expected_code, expected_reason):
    path = root / f"{label}.json"
    path.write_bytes(receipt_bytes)
    argv = [str(GATE), "gate", "--epoch", str(root / "epoch.json"), "--receipt", str(path)]
    result = capture_gate(argv, epoch["repository"])
    response = json.loads(result.stdout if result.returncode == 0 else result.stderr)
    wanted = "ALLOW" if expected_code == 0 else "BLOCK"
    if (result.returncode != expected_code or response["schema_version"] != 3 or response["decision"] != wanted
            or response["reason"] != expected_reason):
        raise ValueError(f"unexpected admission result for {label}: {response}")
    if wanted == "ALLOW" and any(response[key] != epoch[key] for key in ("subject_digest", "policy_digest")):
        raise ValueError("admission returned a different subject or policy")
    return {"case": label, "exit": result.returncode, "response": response}


def replay(epoch, inputs):
    freeze_argv = freeze(epoch)
    receipt = json.loads(inputs["receipt"])
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="semctx-proof-replay.") as scratch:
        root = Path(scratch)
        (root / "epoch.json").write_bytes(inputs["epoch"])
        wrong_subject = receipt | {"subject_digest": "sha256:" + "0" * 64}
        altered = copy.deepcopy(receipt)
        altered["witnesses"][0]["evidence"]["red_stdout"] += "\ncontrolled alteration\n"
        records = [
            gate_check(root, epoch, "stale-receipt", json.dumps(wrong_subject).encode(), 2,
                       "receipt subject does not match the current candidate epoch"),
            gate_check(root, epoch, "altered-witness", json.dumps(altered).encode(), 2,
                       "evidence digest does not match its structured content"),
            gate_check(root, epoch, "original-receipt", inputs["receipt"], 0, "PROOF_ADEQUATE"),
        ]
    return {
        "subject_digest": epoch["subject_digest"], "policy_digest": epoch["policy_digest"],
        "receipt_sha256": digest(inputs["receipt"]), "gate_sha256": GATE_SHA256, "freeze_argv": freeze_argv,
        "checks": records, "qualification_credit": 0,
    }


def review_flags(catalog):
    flags = []
    for feature in DISABLED_FEATURES:
        flags.extend(("--disable", feature))
    for key, value in (
        ("model_catalog_json", str(catalog)), ("model", MODEL), ("sandbox_mode", "read-only"),
        ("mcp_servers.code_intelligence.enabled", False), ("mcp_servers.linear.enabled", False),
        ("apps._default.enabled", False), ("agents.enabled", False), ("web_search", "disabled"),
    ):
        flags.extend(("-c", f"{key}={json.dumps(value)}"))
    return flags


def prepare_review(root, cwd):
    version = checked(capture([str(CODEX), "--version"], cwd=cwd), "Codex version").decode().strip()
    if version != CODEX_VERSION:
        raise ValueError(f"review profile requires {CODEX_VERSION}, got {version}")
    argv = [str(CODEX), "debug", "models", "--bundled"]
    catalog = json.loads(checked(capture(argv, cwd=cwd), "bundled Codex model catalogue"))
    if sum(model["slug"] == MODEL for model in catalog["models"]) != 1:
        raise ValueError("the review model is unavailable in the pinned CLI")
    for model in catalog["models"]:
        model.update(apply_patch_tool_type=None, experimental_supported_tools=[],
                     multi_agent_version="disabled", tool_mode="direct")
    path = root / "review-catalog.json"
    path.write_text(json.dumps(catalog, indent=2) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    flags = review_flags(path)
    argv = [str(CODEX), "-a", "never", "debug", "prompt-input", *flags, "Audit tool inventory."]
    result = capture(argv, cwd=cwd)
    tools = verify_tool_inventory(json.loads(checked(result, "tool inventory")))
    if result.stderr.strip():
        raise ValueError("review tool inventory produced a diagnostic")
    return flags, {
        "cli_version": version, "model": MODEL, "catalog_sha256": digest(path.read_bytes()),
        "declared_tools": tools, "inventory_argv": argv,
    }


def review(epoch, inputs, root, *, launch, case_sha256):
    prior = replay(epoch, inputs) if launch and "receipt" in inputs else None
    freeze_argv = prior["freeze_argv"] if prior else freeze(epoch)
    root.mkdir(mode=0o700)
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="semctx-clean-review.") as cwd:
        flags, record = prepare_review(root, cwd)
        record.update(case_sha256=case_sha256, subject_digest=epoch["subject_digest"], freeze_argv=freeze_argv)
        if launch:
            argv = [
                str(CODEX), "-a", "never", "exec", "--strict-config", "--ephemeral",
                "--skip-git-repo-check", "--sandbox", "read-only", "--cd", cwd,
                *flags, "--json", "--color", "never", "-",
            ]
            record["prior_receipt_sha256"] = prior["receipt_sha256"] if prior else None
            record = record | run_audit(argv, cwd, root, inputs["review_input"])
            freeze(epoch)
        (root / "REVIEW.json").write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
        return record


def run_audit(argv, cwd, root, prompt):
    schema = root / "review-report.schema.json"
    schema.write_text(json.dumps({
        "type": "object", "additionalProperties": False,
        "required": ["findings", "declared_tools", "capabilities"],
        "properties": {
            "findings": {"type": "string"},
            "declared_tools": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}},
            "capabilities": {
                "type": "object", "additionalProperties": False,
                "required": ["execute", "write", "delegate"],
                "properties": {key: {"type": "boolean"} for key in ("execute", "write", "delegate")},
            },
        },
    }), encoding="utf-8")
    prompt += (
        b"\nReturn the structured audit report. In declared_tools list only the current tool declarations, "
        b"with namespace prefixes. In capabilities record whether they allow job execution, "
        b"filesystem, external or goal-state writes, or delegation. Base this on your own current inventory. "
        b"Report uncertainty in findings and set the affected capability to true. Do not call tools.\n"
    )
    argv = [*argv[:-1], "--output-schema", str(schema), "-"]
    result = capture(argv, cwd=cwd, data=prompt, timeout=180)
    (root / "review.events.jsonl").write_bytes(result.stdout)
    (root / "review.stderr").write_bytes(result.stderr)
    events = [json.loads(line) for line in checked(result, "fresh review").splitlines()]
    thread, report = interpret_audit(events)
    return {
        "audit_argv": argv, "review_thread_id": thread, "prompt_sha256": digest(prompt),
        "events_sha256": digest(result.stdout), "stderr_sha256": digest(result.stderr),
        "review_report": report, "qualification_credit": 0,
    }


def interpret_audit(events):
    phases = [event["type"] for event in events]
    categories = {"thread.started", "turn.started", "item.started", "item.updated", "item.completed", "turn.completed"}
    if (not phases or phases[0] != "thread.started" or phases[-1] != "turn.completed"
            or phases.count("turn.started") != 1 or set(phases) - categories):
        raise ValueError("fresh review had an unexpected event sequence")
    thread_ids = [event["thread_id"] for event in events if event["type"] == "thread.started"]
    if (len(thread_ids) != 1 or not isinstance(thread_ids[0], str) or not thread_ids[0].strip()
            or phases.count("turn.completed") != 1):
        raise ValueError("fresh review did not complete")
    items = [event["item"] for event in events if "item" in event]
    if any(item["type"].endswith("_call") or item["type"] not in (
        "agent_message", "reasoning", "error"
    ) for item in items):
        raise ValueError("review contained an unexpected tool or action")
    findings = [event["item"]["text"] for event in events[phases.index("turn.started") + 1:-1]
                if event["type"] == "item.completed" and event["item"]["type"] == "agent_message"]
    if len(findings) != 1:
        raise ValueError("review did not produce one completed findings message")
    if any(item["type"] == "error" and not item.get("message", "").startswith(
        "clamping SessionEnd hook timeout"
    ) for item in items):
        raise ValueError("review reported an unexpected runtime error")
    report = json.loads(findings[0])
    if (not report["findings"].strip() or tuple(report["declared_tools"]) != PLAN_TOOL
            or report["capabilities"] != {"execute": False, "write": False, "delegate": False}):
        raise ValueError("the fresh reviewer did not confirm its restricted capabilities")
    return thread_ids[0], report


def main():
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
    parser.add_argument("--case", type=Path, default=HERE / "case.json")
    parser.add_argument("--case-sha256", help="Expected manifest SHA-256 for a different case.")
    commands = parser.add_subparsers(dest="command", required=True)
    commands.add_parser("replay", help="Verify the prior receipt and negative controls offline.")
    for name, help_text in [
        ("check-review", "Freeze the candidate and verify the Codex tool inventory locally."),
        ("audit", "Start a new Codex review in the verified read-only profile."),
    ]:
        command = commands.add_parser(name, help=help_text)
        command.add_argument("--output", type=Path, required=True)
    args = parser.parse_args()
    try:
        case = args.case.resolve(strict=True)
        expected = DEFAULT_CASE_SHA256 if case == HERE / "case.json" else args.case_sha256
        if expected is None:
            raise ValueError("a different proof case requires --case-sha256")
        epoch, inputs = load_case(case, expected)
        if args.command == "replay":
            report = replay(epoch, inputs) | {"case_sha256": expected}
        else:
            report = review(epoch, inputs, args.output.resolve(), launch=args.command == "audit",
                            case_sha256=expected)
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as error:
        parser.exit(2, f"{error}\n")
    print(json.dumps(report, indent=2))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()


